{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline","id":165114,"title":"Kerberos Bloodline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-10T13:50:53-07:00","id":165114,"title":"Kerberos Bloodline","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-jaws-of-the-beast/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/the-jaws-of-the-beast/</a><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">What do we think?<br /> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T13:59:33-07:00","id":165135,"title":"","content":"I like them a lot, since, one of my favorite things is the Predatory Aura. I think the one thing I'm wishing is that they had a Bloodline Bane that was more distinctive and cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T14:02:42-07:00","id":165139,"title":"","content":"Finally the Gangrel have that can play toe to toe with the Deva and Venture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T14:15:03-07:00","id":165147,"title":"","content":"I feel like the Kerberos and the Taifa are two examples where they should be able to, though I think the Taifa need an update.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T14:16:33-07:00","id":165149,"title":"","content":"I like the focus on the Beast and Predatory Aura, and find their bloodline weakness to be interesting. Plus, an intriguing merit. I know people like more disciplines (one of the complaints I heard about Werewolf lodges was that they were worthless because they didn't all give gift trees) but I think there's more ways to establish a variance of supernatural focus than with a discipline. The theme behind khaibit devotions and the neglatu abilities and now this merit are showing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T14:20:21-07:00","id":165153,"title":"","content":"Could someone explain that second dot of the merit to me? Does the once a month limit still apply?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T14:20:27-07:00","id":165154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=165147#post165147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the Kerberos and the Taifa are two examples where they should be able to, though I think the Taifa need an update.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm tempted to use this <i>as</i> the Taifa update - this bloodline weakness makes much more sense to me than their 'pack oriented' one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T14:34:42-07:00","id":165200,"title":"","content":"The Taifa could be a particular lineage of the Kerberos.<br /> <br /> I think the second dot weirds me out because it sounds sort of gamey. Kerberos become beat machines or something.<br /> <br /> Y'know, since the Kerberos make heavy use of Predatory Aura, it kind of stinks that it can only be applied once a month.<br /> <br /> Another question, how do the Predatory Aura Conditions make you feel? Are they overwhelmingly urgent (That seems like it might be irritating if you're stuck with it for days as a result of a single roll) Or can they have a more subtle effect? Like is a character who got hit with Competitive by a BP5 Elder just gonna be up in everybody's grille for five days, or how would you characterize it so it isn't ridiculous?<br /> <br /> Still feeling like the once a month thing is a bit weird, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 06-10-2014, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T15:02:04-07:00","id":165239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=165200#post165200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another question, how do the Predatory Aura Conditions make you feel? Are they overwhelmingly urgent (That seems like it might be irritating if you're stuck with it for days as a result of a single roll) Or can they have a more subtle effect? Like is a character who got hit with Competitive by a BP5 Elder just gonna be up in everybody's grille for five days, or how would you characterize it so it isn't ridiculous?</div> </div> </div> </div>A predatory aura Condition is like a mood you can't quite shake. You won't be getting in everyone's face, but you'll keep getting this itch to call people on their bullshit, or better yet, show them up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T17:31:26-07:00","id":165425,"title":"","content":"I think the second merit dot needs work as well. As it's written, you seem to be able to take the condition at any time, including just as you complete the required resolving factor. For instance, you could spend an entire fight fighting normally, and then suddenly decide &quot;Hey, I've got Bestial now!&quot; on the exact swing that will deal damage in the last 3 boxes (not too hard to calculate). Or gain Competitive at the end of a contest (it says &quot;win or lose&quot;, not &quot;win or lose a contest during which you had this condition the entire time...&quot;). Bit weird.<br /> <br /> I love their style, but in the campaign I'm in I generally get willpower back so slowly that an ability dependent on spending wp versus vampires would be a tough sell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T01:27:42-07:00","id":165722,"title":"","content":"How does this ability make the Kerberos uniquely qualified to judge someone's worthiness to sire or be considered a candidate for the Embrace?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T01:30:14-07:00","id":165723,"title":"","content":"The question begging: how do they relate to the Cult of Set and Khaibits ? I mean.. is their Typhon the same &quot;Typhon-Set&quot; ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T02:07:41-07:00","id":165738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=165722#post165722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does this ability make the Kerberos uniquely qualified to judge someone's worthiness to sire or be considered a candidate for the Embrace?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Simple.. you lash out upon the would be childe with your beast and you see how can he handle these conditions. After all, the childe must be ready to fight the beast, so if he can't handle a few very weak conditions (in comparison with the beasts nudging you all the time) then you are unworthy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T02:32:08-07:00","id":165743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=165723#post165723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question begging: how do they relate to the Cult of Set and Khaibits ? I mean.. is their Typhon the same &quot;Typhon-Set&quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, maybe not... As always with nWoD.<br /> <br /> It is probably some derivative of or variation on <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Typhon\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T04:48:29-07:00","id":165797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=165738#post165738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Simple.. you lash out upon the would be childe with your beast and you see how can he handle these conditions. After all, the childe must be ready to fight the beast, so if he can't handle a few very weak conditions (in comparison with the beasts nudging you all the time) then you are unworthy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any vampire can already do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T08:16:47-07:00","id":165932,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but because of their style which enhances their lashing out, they're particularly vicious, so standing up to them is a particular challenge.<br /> <br /> I imagine it was about testing sires, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T15:47:25-07:00","id":166298,"title":"","content":"Is this supposed to be an example of one of those failed bloodlines? In that it doesn't doesn't quite live up to the role the inceptor chose for it. Because they're not inherently better at getting any character insight or making a character judgement call than any other (insert clan type here) who decides to fling around their predatory aura and watching what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T15:57:02-07:00","id":166304,"title":"","content":"I think that's mistakenly conflating a metaphysical significance with a social role. Perhaps among the ancient Greek Kindred, there was some sort of trial by fire involving the Predatory Aura that had to be passed before you could sire. The Kerberos might insist that their relationship with the Beast accords them a greater ability to test the applicants because they provide a better challenge, therefore making them the best at choosing who sires and who doesn't.<br /> <br /> I don't really think it has anything to do with a magical clan sorting hat ability or anything like that. They fit that social role within the Greek Kindred hierarchy. They facilitated their political savvy through the application of their auras/their facility for Majesty. Hence why this bloodline rose to prominence as opposed to another lineage in that social position.<br /> <br /> When they weren't among the Greeks or the Greeks decided they preferred less rigid rules for siring, the Kerberos supposedly adapted, finding other political rolls to function in. Hence that part of the write up. I don't get the impression they failed, things changed, so they changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T16:06:15-07:00","id":166309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=166298#post166298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this supposed to be an example of one of those failed bloodlines? In that it doesn't doesn't quite live up to the role the inceptor chose for it. Because they're not inherently better at getting any character insight or making a character judgement call than any other (insert clan type here) who decides to fling around their predatory aura and watching what happens.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They keep naive neonates from Embracing all their friends and family and ancilla from Embracing anyone who might assist them on a political front by sheer force of Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T16:06:46-07:00","id":166310,"title":"","content":"Predators that excel in the survival of the fittest role is what I got from them. They definitely can fill whatever niche they need to by adapting that Predatory Aura, which I think is a really kickass concept. <br /> <br /> I hope there is some more filler on that whole Typhon-aspect of them though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>\u201cAnd those who were seen dancing were thought to be insane by those who could not hear the music.\u201d - Friedrich Nietzsche</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/812-datura","name":"Datura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T17:19:41-07:00","id":166369,"title":"","content":"The bonus dice to predatory aura makes them pretty powerful honestly, especially in challenging would-be Childer, even more so than prospective sires. Acquiring a consistent bonus to predatory aura like this (equivalent to increasing a physical trait in regard to that aspect), for a rather low cost (1 xp per dot) and gaining significant social bonuses if their BP is higher can provide a great deal of challenge and insight into the prospective childe.<br /> <br /> You can even essentially dominate using the merit, its pretty powerful in social and other challenges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T05:25:00-07:00","id":167775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=166369#post166369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bonus dice to predatory aura makes them pretty powerful honestly, especially in challenging would-be Childer, even more so than prospective sires. Acquiring a consistent bonus to predatory aura like this (equivalent to increasing a physical trait in regard to that aspect), for a rather low cost (1 xp per dot) and gaining significant social bonuses if their BP is higher can provide a great deal of challenge and insight into the prospective childe.<br /> <br /> You can even essentially dominate using the merit, its pretty powerful in social and other challenges.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not to mention? Significant advantage to resisting uses of Majesty / Nightmare through Lashing Out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-14T05:27:18-07:00","id":168807,"title":"","content":"I was pleasantly surprised to read the Typhon mention. One of my last games was set in Athens and a custom hunter compact I wrote and used were the Guardians of the Vineyard. Both Ekhidna and Typhon featured heavily in their mythos. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A vile creature poisoned the ancient and sacred vineyards of Dionysus, for She wished to claim the gardens as her own and sustain her dark children on the sweet nectar that was the wine-God's greatest gift to Humanity. Dionysus petitioned to Zeus for help against the forces of darkness. The Olympian chose to ignore his pleas, for Echidna was the daughter of Tartarus -warden of imprisoned Titans. Only when the Mother, her mate Ixion-Typhon and their blasphemous offspring assaulted Olympus and stole immortality, did the Father of Gods and Mortals take action. Ixion-Typhon was bound to a fiery wheel that would never cease spinning, and was imprisoned deep within a volcano. The Mother and her children were allowed to flee Zeus' terrible wrath, to challenge the worth of all future great warriors. We are those Heroes and Heroines. We still seek out the Dark Mother's wretched children, driving them out and reclaiming the sacred vineyards. We will cut their heads off as they feed from the sweet and holy wine of Dionysus, that is the blood of Humanity. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 06-14-2014, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T09:58:08-07:00","id":169872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=165723#post165723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question begging: how do they relate to the Cult of Set and Khaibits ? I mean.. is their Typhon the same &amp;quot;Typhon-Set&amp;quot; ?</div> </div> </div> </div> Set, the Egyptian god was often associated with Typhon, the Greek monster. Whether or not there is any genuine connection is pretty much up to the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T13:30:34-07:00","id":189605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=166369#post166369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bonus dice to predatory aura makes them pretty powerful honestly, especially in challenging would-be Childer, even more so than prospective sires. Acquiring a consistent bonus to predatory aura like this (equivalent to increasing a physical trait in regard to that aspect), for a rather low cost (1 xp per dot) and gaining significant social bonuses if their BP is higher can provide a great deal of challenge and insight into the prospective childe.<br /> <br /> You can even essentially dominate using the merit, its pretty powerful in social and other challenges.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Please forgive the necro, but don't style merits work like old disciplines? They are a group of merits you must buy in order so its 1xp for the first + 2xp for the second and so on, totaling 15xp for the whole tree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3242,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3242-lddstyx","user":"LddStyx","date":".  spelling 07-06-2014, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3242-lddstyx","name":"LddStyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T13:34:37-07:00","id":189611,"title":"","content":"They don't. Everything post Blood &amp; Smoke is flat costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T14:09:56-07:00","id":189628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LddStyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=189605#post189605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Please forgive the necro, but don't style merits work like old disciplines? They are a group of merits you must buy in order so its 1xp for the first + 2xp for the second and so on, totaling 15xp for the whole tree.</div> </div> </div> </div> The wording in GMC about having to buy each dot of a style Merit in order has caused a lot of people to make this mistake. No, they're still flat costs like everything in 2DRR, but you can't learn a maneuver unless you've learned all of the previous maneuvers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T18:05:58-07:00","id":189726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=189628#post189628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The wording in GMC about having to buy each dot of a style Merit in order has caused a lot of people to make this mistake. No, they're still flat costs like everything in 2DRR, but you can't learn a maneuver unless you've learned all of the previous maneuvers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi,<br /> <br /> Is it basically the same as Status, Professional Training or Cult? Is there an official errata? <br /> If Style Merits work like the new Disciplines then it\u00b4s impossible to learn a maneuver unless you learn all the previous maneuvers. Then the rule isn't &quot;can't learn a Maneuver unless you've learned all of the previous Maneuvers&quot; it's &quot;if you buy the 5th dot Maneuver you get all previous Maneuvers along with it&quot;<br /> <br /> Nitpick: All maneuvers having a <b>Name (Dots) </b>format instead of Professions/Cults &quot;Dots Name:&quot; block of benefits makes them seem like merits that are just hooked into a chain where every Maneuver has the previous Maneuver as a prerequisite. Also were they were balanced on improve-by-one-increment basis?<br /> Any 5 Dot Maneuver feels like it could be a stand-alone Merit... Although comparing to Cult Initiation that gives you 2*1 Dot Merits, a 2 Dot Merit, 2*3 Dot Merits and misc. benefits for up to 10+xp of value, but requiring an outside organisation to purely innate knowledge that any Style represents for a total of 15xp of value, is maybe balanced... :/<br /> Also that means a Kerberos gets a 4 die advantage in Lash out rolls against a similar character that bought 1BP for that 5xp <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Oh, wait... it\u00b4s a tie with 5 dots of Hunting Grounds... hmm.. *jots down &quot;Never meet a Kerberos outside own territory&quot;* :P<br /> <br /> Thank you for the quick reply,<br /> Styx<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3242-lddstyx","name":"LddStyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T23:23:40-07:00","id":189965,"title":"","content":"It doesn't need an Errata. Also, it takes 5 exp to get all 5 maneuvers of a 5 dot merit. Each dot only costs 1 exp for merits. You don't buy fighting styles maneuver by maneuver, you never did, you always had to progress through the lower dots.<br /> <br /> Each dot costs the exact same amount of exp as the dot before it and the dot after it.<br /> <br /> Fighting styles requiring previous dots is nothing new.<br /> <br /> Cult Initiation doesn't cost 15 exp for all of its dots, it costs 5.<br /> <br /> The new costs aren't X New Dots. They're flat costs. The first dot of a merit costs 1 exp, the second dot costs 1 exp, etc. They all cost 1 exp.<br /> <br /> 1-5 dots in any merit, style or otherwise is just 5 exp. Each Maneuver isn't its own Merit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T00:13:47-07:00","id":189990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=189965#post189965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't need an Errata. Also, it takes 5 exp to get all 5 maneuvers of a 5 dot merit. Each dot only costs 1 exp for merits. You don't buy fighting styles maneuver by maneuver, you never did, you always had to progress through the lower dots.<br /> <br /> Each dot costs the exact same amount of exp as the dot before it and the dot after it.<br /> <br /> Fighting styles requiring previous dots is nothing new.<br /> <br /> Cult Initiation doesn't cost 15 exp for all of its dots, it costs 5.<br /> <br /> The new costs aren't X New Dots. They're flat costs. The first dot of a merit costs 1 exp, the second dot costs 1 exp, etc. They all cost 1 exp.<br /> <br /> 1-5 dots in any merit, style or otherwise is just 5 exp. Each Maneuver isn't its own Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was at no point confused by Cult Initiation. As it was in the nitpick part, that is, a different point being made. I was drawing the comparison to Cult Initiation precisely because Cult Initiation cost 5xp total for 10+xp worth of powers. Followed by musing on game balance ending with a conclusion that it just might be balanced that way.<br /> <br /> The point was that Style Merits don't need any special mentions nor should should it have a special layout. In a system where it's bought incrementally the &quot;can't learn a Maneuver unless you've learned all of the previous Maneuvers&quot; is a logically incoherent statement. It highlights a system exception that does <i>not</i> exist. It by its very nature as a non sequitur does not inform and therefore fails its sole propose of clarification and has no reason for existence. The correct rule should be &quot;when you buy the xth dot of X Style you can use Maneuvers up to x&quot; or &quot;if you buy the 5th dot Maneuver you get all previous Maneuvers along with it&quot; or &quot;you buy dots in the Style Merit, not Maneuvers&quot;<br /> <br /> I am coming from the book standpoint not forum acknowledged/corrected viewpoint. I am critically pointing out the logical conclusion any non-forum goer would draw from the free rules update.<br /> <br /> But this is probably not the place for this discussion.<br /> <br /> Addendum: Compare Fast-Talking, a non-style merit to any style merit. I would say it is a Style merit in all, but the keyword. But lacking the special rule, I'd buy it sequential like the new disciplines or as Cacophony Savvy puts it &quot;each level builds on the previous&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3242,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3242-lddstyx","user":"LddStyx","date":".  Addendum 07-07-2014, 03:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3242-lddstyx","name":"LddStyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T09:20:18-07:00","id":190392,"title":"","content":"You do know that Disciplines also only cost 3-4 exp each time you raise them right? And you never picked and chose which levels you bought?<br /> <br /> Nothings changed there except there are only flat costs. You NEVER EVER in the system multiply the cost by the dots.<br /> <br /> To buy 1-5 in an in clan discipline, you pay 15 exp. 3 for the first dot, 3 for the second, etc.<br /> <br /> You keep mentioning 'like disciplines' but disciplines don't work any different than anything else in the way the dots are bought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T15:07:31-07:00","id":190779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=190392#post190392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do know that Disciplines also only cost 3-4 exp each time you raise them right? And you never picked and chose which levels you bought?<br /> <br /> Nothings changed there except there are only flat costs. You NEVER EVER in the system multiply the cost by the dots.<br /> <br /> To buy 1-5 in an in clan discipline, you pay 15 exp. 3 for the first dot, 3 for the second, etc.<br /> <br /> You keep mentioning 'like disciplines' but disciplines don't work any different than anything else in the way the dots are bought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please note that I differentiate between new disciplines and old disciplines in different posts. I have been informed already about the fact that all traits have a flat cost after GMG.<br /> <br /> My nitpick is with the wording &quot;Each maneuver is a prerequisite for the next in its sequence.&quot; p.158 GMRU alongside the use of &quot;prerequisite&quot; as a Merit system term e.g. some Merits prerequisite other Merits.<br /> <br /> My question is, why are Style Merits a special kind of thing needing special mention and a special rule, when they aren't and the rule is the same as for everything else? Is this rule clarifying anything? Am I misunderstanding logic or the English language? Am I to assume &quot;If the prerequisites mention a covenant, the Merit requires a single dot of the appropriate Covenant Status to purchase.&quot; p.109 B&amp;S means that the Covenant Status is free. I think not.<br /> <br /> To reiterate I know the costs don't scale with the number of dots bought in the post-GMC nWoD. What I am arguing for is clarity of meaning in the wording of rules. Style Merits can be misconstrued (as I did at first, but not any more) self-contained Merit trees. E<span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">mphasis of flat costs does nothing to alleviate this, if they are seen as separate Merits instead of <i>benefits</i> of the <u><i>one</i></u> Style merit.<br /> <br /> PM me if you have any more questions about my argument.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3242-lddstyx","name":"LddStyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3242_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-07T17:39:20-07:00","id":190967,"title":"","content":"Cult initiation is very powerful, as is professional training. The St should take steps to balance it by requiring the IC fluff to be met. Cult initiation means you're part of a cult, with all the problems that entails. Professional training requires you to continue doing that profession, keeping up your network and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T11:47:53-07:00","id":191575,"title":"","content":"I think the bloodline is good, but not excessively so. I mean you get your blood potency as bonus to rolls pursuing your beast aspect after you defeat another when lashing out. So if its a draw or the other chooses the flight option nothing extraordianry happens (without the merit).<br /> Also do note that you have to pick the merit for each different aspect of the beast, which I think goes a long way in making the bloodline more... tame. Even when inflicting the subservient condition its only for commands that align to the specific beast aspect.<br /> <br /> The only thing that confuses me is the whole inflict upon yourself the bestial conditions. If you have resolved them in the last month its impossible to inflict them again. Right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2024-malfi","name":"Malfi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T12:05:41-07:00","id":191593,"title":"","content":"I don't like that dot because it serves no purpose besides generating Beats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T15:29:36-07:00","id":191732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=191593#post191593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like that dot because it serves no purpose besides generating Beats.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No it serves another purpose. It makes the Kereberos immune at will to being subjected to the respective conditions of losing to another for Lashing out even if they would have gotten their ass handed to them by someone they tried to slap around who had the Cutthroat, Enticing, or Atrocious merits. Not only do they get a cheap counter to a series of merits, but they get xp for using such a cheesy tactic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T03:41:58-07:00","id":192229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=191732#post191732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No it serves another purpose. It makes the Kereberos immune at will to being subjected to the respective conditions of losing to another for Lashing out even if they would have gotten their ass handed to them by someone they tried to slap around who had the Cutthroat, Enticing, or Atrocious merits. Not only do they get a cheap counter to a series of merits, but they get xp for using such a cheesy tactic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> nop, that doesn't give you full immunity. You just become immune to the condition.. the +2 bonus for winning still works (unless you use flight.. but then the opponent won anyways)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T14:36:26-07:00","id":253595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=165200#post165200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y'know, since the Kerberos make heavy use of Predatory Aura, it kind of stinks that it can only be applied once a month.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=165153#post165153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the once a month limit still apply?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bestial, Competitive and Wanton conditions have the once a month restrictions associated with them and not Predatory Aura. This means while you may be able to actually apply an aura to someone as many times as you are capable of trying, you might not be able to afflict their associated conditions on them, but they are 100% affected by the rest of the aura.<br /> <br /> \u200bCowing (the three dot) allows you to apply Subservient in place of the other conditions for being successful. Subservient does not have the once a month restriction that Bestial, Competitive and Wanton have, so you can apply as many times as you are allowed attempts against a person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T15:06:35-07:00","id":253619,"title":"","content":"Internalizing (the two dot) for The Three Heads of Kerberos actually makes a lot of sense and allows a character to inoculate herself against the Bestial, Competitive and Wonton conditions in a controlled environment. This makes a lot sense to do because this bloodline is going to lash out more than any other kindred and expose themselves to being lashed out against in retaliation and possibly lose.<br /> <br /> The beat part of the merit make sense since Kerberos are much closer to their beast and they use it to gain a better understanding of themselves and their beast, whereas any other vampire is simply weakened by it. It is worth pointing out that there are other merits that grant beats when certain circumstances are met, and I am sure more will be written.<br /> <br /> You must consider the drawbacks of the Bestial, Competitive and Wanton Conditions, and they are very sever and difficult to resolve, making it more likely they are going to mess themselves up in the process of getting that beat. In reality they are more likely to mess themselves up and fail at getting that beat than they are to succeed.<br /> <br /> A good storyteller will make a player using Internalizing actually earn the beats while making the process engaging. A bad or lazy ST will simply hand out the beats.<br /> <br /> The Balance is there. Internalize represents the theme of the Kerberos. Most importantly it promotes creative play and storytelling. This merit should stay the way it is written.<br /> <br /> I also forgot to mention that no one wants someone else's beast being used on them, even if they are trying to get a benefit from it. Not only is it unpleasant, it leaves witness that are aware of your weakened state. These witnesses may try to sell that information to others, be forced to give that information up, exploit it themselves, among many other horrible things that could happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1852,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","user":"Maskah","date":". 09-09-2014, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T15:15:32-07:00","id":253626,"title":"","content":"I thought it worth mentioning that The Hound of Hell is actually a weakness if you are BP 1 and meaningless if you are BP2. The way it is currently written it gives you a +1 at BP1, which is lower than the normal +2. At BP2 you get +2, which is exactly the same as the +2 you would normally get.<br /> For this to actually be a benefit it should be a bonus equal to 1 + BP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T16:06:25-07:00","id":253652,"title":"","content":"Considering how Typhon was described to look like? I'm curious to see what forms they take with Protean. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T16:54:50-07:00","id":253674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=253652#post253652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering how Typhon was described to look like? I'm curious to see what forms they take with Protean. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can see the bloodline developing devotions to manifest the aspects of Typhon. Bloodlines often do that in order to support their legends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T17:54:26-07:00","id":253701,"title":"","content":"&quot;Come on Gangrel, turn into a beast!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>A beast?</b> Bitch, I can turn into <b>every</b> <b>beast</b>!&quot;<br /> <br /> Hah!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T19:15:26-07:00","id":253762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maskah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=253626#post253626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it worth mentioning that The Hound of Hell is actually a weakness if you are BP 1 and meaningless if you are BP2. The way it is currently written it gives you a +1 at BP1, which is lower than the normal +2. At BP2 you get +2, which is exactly the same as the +2 you would normally get.<br /> For this to actually be a benefit it should be a bonus equal to 1 + BP.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are two parts of the Hound of Hell benefit. The first part really doesn't become a benefit until BP3. But you can always add your dots to lash out attempts. I didn't explicitly state this, but it's a benefit that becomes more beneficial later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T22:48:04-07:00","id":253851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=253762#post253762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There are two parts of the Hound of Hell benefit. The first part really doesn't become a benefit until BP3. But you can always add your dots to lash out attempts. I didn't explicitly state this, but it's a benefit that becomes more beneficial later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I noticed that. In the new system you can get a bloodline at BP 1, meaning this is a penalty and a weakness until BP2 and no real benefit until BP3. In your description of The Hound of Hell you wrote, &quot;This advantage (birthright), gives the Kerberos an edge in any interactions with the beast.&quot; I strongly feel that my minor tweak is balanced and does away with an unnecessary penalty that does not make sense and even better matches that description.<br /> <br /> Outside of that I thought the mechanics for the bloodline were very solid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T11:51:14-07:00","id":255458,"title":"","content":"It is worth mentioning that a GM can take the option of earning beats away from the 2nd dots. I know a lot of GM's that like to control the pace of XP in their games so focus is not taken off Roleplaying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T13:24:43-07:00","id":257532,"title":"","content":"Lashing Out cost 1 willpower to use against Vampires which would mean that the 4th dot of the bloodline merit cannot be used against Vampires. Is this intentional?<br /> <br /> Can the 5th dot only affect one Kindred?<br /> <br /> As far as I am aware you can only spend 1 Willpower a turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T13:39:11-07:00","id":257557,"title":"","content":"You need a Willpower to fight back against someone with higher Blood Potency, but not otherwise.<br /> <br /> So I imagine they can't use it on people with more potent blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T15:17:48-07:00","id":257653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=257557#post257557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need a Willpower to fight back against someone with higher Blood Potency, but not otherwise.<br /> <br /> So I imagine they can't use it on people with more potent blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must have been reading a typo in my B&amp;S PDF. Thanks for the clarity!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T16:13:09-07:00","id":257673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=257557#post257557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need a Willpower to fight back against someone with higher Blood Potency, but not otherwise.<br /> <br /> So I imagine they can't use it on people with more potent blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can't use it to fight back if the vampire has more potent blood, any other use should be ok. Am i wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T17:13:53-07:00","id":257698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TittoPaolo210</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=257673#post257673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can't use it to fight back if the vampire has more potent blood, any other use should be ok. Am i wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to use the Kerberos ability that costs Willpower, you can't use that to fight back against a Kindred with higher BP, because you've already spent your Willpower for the turn.<br /> <br /> If you're just fighting back against the higher BP Kindred, you just need to spend the WP and hope your dice like you more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T12:15:31-08:00","id":430483,"title":"","content":"#Threadcromancy!<br /> <br /> Considering that a Kerberos will have to fling around a lot of Willpower to use their abilities (or they'll constantly be at a disadvantage vs other Kindred\u2014it's almost like constantly having the Competitive condition), would the second dot of their merit be better served by helping refresh that?<br /> <br /> Also, given that a subjugated Kindred is immune to said Predatory Aura infliction again for a month, this sounds like the Kerberos would get a quick bonus, but then their Bane would be a constant problem vs that same target\u2014you get to show off briefly, then you're stuck unable to get 10-Again\u2014for the rest of the month. It hardly seems like they're &quot;wielding the Predatory Aura as if it's second nature&quot; if they can't really sustain it.<br /> <br /> A couple of alternatives to Internalization:<br /> <br /> Idea 1a: If they succeed (or score exceptional success perhaps?) on the Predatory Aura challenge, the Kerberos regains the Willpower they spent to initiate it.<br /> <br /> Idea 1b: If they succeed (or score exceptionally?) on the Predatory Aura, they gain the Inspired condition in relation to the challenge.<br /> <br /> Idea 2: If they succeed (or score exceptionally?) on the Predatory Aura, their Bane does not apply vs the target for that month, while the target is, of course, unable to be affected by anyone else trying the same aura. This would also mean that if someone else has already inflicted one of the three conditions on a subject, they're &quot;immunized&quot; to the Kerberos' own attempts to show dominance over them; e.g. If their target's already been hit with Bestial by a third party, said Kerberos can't hold back their Bane by pushing the Bestial condition on them. (This would apply even if the target was inflicted with Subservient, since the dice-rolling and the type of related aura would otherwise be the same; I can imagine a pecking order of who controls whom being established by multiple Kerberoi in this sort of situation.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 03-06-2015, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T12:25:18-07:00","id":442942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zsander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/165114-kerberos-bloodline?p=430483#post430483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">#Threadcromancy!<br /> <br /> Considering that a Kerberos will have to fling around a lot of Willpower to use their abilities (or they'll constantly be at a disadvantage vs other Kindred\u2014it's almost like constantly having the Competitive condition), would the second dot of their merit be better served by helping refresh that?<br /> <br /> Also, given that a subjugated Kindred is immune to said Predatory Aura infliction again for a month, this sounds like the Kerberos would get a quick bonus, but then their Bane would be a constant problem vs that same target\u2014you get to show off briefly, then you're stuck unable to get 10-Again\u2014for the rest of the month. It hardly seems like they're &quot;wielding the Predatory Aura as if it's second nature&quot; if they can't really sustain it.<br /> <br /> A couple of alternatives to Internalization:<br /> <br /> Idea 1a: If they succeed (or score exceptional success perhaps?) on the Predatory Aura challenge, the Kerberos regains the Willpower they spent to initiate it.<br /> <br /> Idea 1b: If they succeed (or score exceptionally?) on the Predatory Aura, they gain the Inspired condition in relation to the challenge.<br /> <br /> Idea 2: If they succeed (or score exceptionally?) on the Predatory Aura, their Bane does not apply vs the target for that month, while the target is, of course, unable to be affected by anyone else trying the same aura. This would also mean that if someone else has already inflicted one of the three conditions on a subject, they're &quot;immunized&quot; to the Kerberos' own attempts to show dominance over them; e.g. If their target's already been hit with Bestial by a third party, said Kerberos can't hold back their Bane by pushing the Bestial condition on them. (This would apply even if the target was inflicted with Subservient, since the dice-rolling and the type of related aura would otherwise be the same; I can imagine a pecking order of who controls whom being established by multiple Kerberoi in this sort of situation.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I personally like idea 2 the best. There is already a lot of alternatives for for getting willpower back or getting inspired. It also makes the most sense.<br /> <br /> The way the beat system is that you gain beats for sucking is a terrible idea. I have yet to meet anyone that uses that system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T19:56:11-07:00","id":600125,"title":"","content":"Another idea I had . . .<br /> <br /> Considering their &quot;Masters of the Aura&quot; nature, kerberoi should even be able to stand up to elder kindred, for whatever that's worth.<br /> <br /> How about . . .<br /> <br /> <b>\u25cf\u25cf UNYIELDING</b> Add your points in the Three Heads of Kerberos merit toward your Blood Potency value; if the total meets or exceeds the Blood Potency of another Kindred with a normally higher Blood Potency, Lashing Out in response to a Predatory Aura challenge does not cost you any willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 07-23-2015, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}